Job Description
 Our client seeks a motivated developer to join an international program aiming at deploying a Policy Administration system worldwide, in all the Business Units of the Group.
Within his/her Rollout Team, the candidate will work on rolling out the platform to his designated BU(s), adjusting features, fix defects, be curious about the business needs, be autonomous in his/her work yet confident to ask for help from the team when needed.
Job Responsibilities:
 Uses Spring framework to develop microservices; 
 Uses Aspose library APIs to process documents in popular file formats such as word; 
 Uses version-control systems; 
 Update data stored in the original database from the same front-end applications; 
 Write unit tests; 
 Setting up the insurance product in the application his/her team is part of by means of product parameters; 
 Contribute, by providing analysis and recommendations not directly linked to business requirements with continuous improvement of; 
 The candidate provides technical support to the other members/developers of the feature team; 
 The scope is mainly back-end (Front-end is a small part of the scope). 
 Job Requirements
 Minimum 4 years of experience in Java / Spring; 
 Professional expertise in SQL (stored procedures would be a plus); 
 Experience in Angular would be a plus; 
 Experience of Public Cloud environments, AWS would be a plus; 
 Experience of CI CD pipelines in a DevOps environment; 
 Permanently pursuing excellence in the quality of the code delivered; 
 Team player; 
 Communication and interpersonal skills. 
 This job description outlines the general nature and level of work performed by employees within this classification and is not intended to be a comprehensive inventory of all duties and responsibilities. Additionally, the responsibility to possess the necessary employment documents for this country rests with the candidate.
 What We Offer
 You will find here not only an environment where you can do meaningful work and feel supported, but also a benefits package designed to foster your growth and well-being:
 Soft skills and technical training for current and emerging products and technologies; 
 Mentoring programs that connect you with mentors from around the world; 
 Employee Assistance Programs to support your well-being, both personally and professionally; 
 Career development opportunities to grow within the team; 
 Special referral bonuses for recommending friends; 
 A friendly team eager to welcome you. 
 About Us
 Stefanini is a Brazilian multinational company with 39 years of experience and presence in 41 countries. With more than 35,000 employees, we co-create solutions for a better future, driving digital transformation with a focus on real results.
We operate in an integrated way through 7 specialized business units: Consulting (Technology and Business Agility), Analytics & AI, Banking & Payments, Cybersecurity, Manufacturing 4.0, and Digital Marketing. We are a group that breathes collaboration and offers a dynamic environment where you will learn by doing, grow alongside the team, and have space to contribute with ideas and projects.
If you are looking for a place to develop, innovate, and be part of something bigger, then Stefanini is your place.
